From 78644ab785bf8b1a8cdb1a9e7c81165b3785e61b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph <joseph@giallovision.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Deforum COMP: tempo-locked modulation, prompt sequence,
 seamless loops

Replace Deforum_UI with a `deforum` Base COMP built from schema.py:
every schedulable Deforum parameter at its baseline (float base + raw
override), on Tempo / Globals / Prompts / Motion / Camera & Depth /
Diffusion / Noise & Color / Flow & Anti-blur / Mod Matrix / CN / Pipeline
pages. build_master_ui.py migrates Deforum_UI values on first run.

- tempo.py: bpm/bars/fps -> plan; 60 fps + cadence or low fps + RIFE/FILM
- modulation.py: 8-slot Mod Matrix compiled to comma-free numexpr
  expressions (float divisors: numexpr floor-divides int/int inside
  Deforum); Mod CHOP input baked per frame, loop-normalised
- prompt_seq.py: beat-indexed prompts with crossfades as weighted AND
  prompts (Deforum holds prompts, it does not blend them)
- seamless loops: overlap render, seed schedule s + t%loop, loop player
  (loop_head/loop_tail -> loop_cross) crossfading the seam
- interpolated outputs (<ts>_RIFE|FILM_xN.mp4) auto-load, with fallback
- bake button now previews the compiled schedules (no POST)
- legacy_colormatch baseline on, matching what the API applied before
- tests: Deforum schedule/prompt simulator, builder run against a TD mock

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
